CAT = "sgm5Products"; SEG = "PRD"
Q = [
('Under FAA-N16, a life policy that is NOT investment-linked is generally classed as:',
 'An Excluded Investment Product', ['A Specified Investment Product', 'A listed derivative', 'A collective investment scheme'],
 'Annex 1 of FAA-N16 lists life policies other than investment-linked policies as Excluded Investment Products. ILP sub-funds are Excluded only in the set circumstances.'),
('Any investment product that is not an Excluded Investment Product is a:',
 'Specified Investment Product', ['Prescribed Capital Product', 'Restricted Scheme Product', 'Recognised Fund'],
 'FAA-N16 defines a Specified Investment Product as any investment product other than an Excluded Investment Product. SIPs carry the CKA or CAR safeguards.'),
('In an investment-linked policy, the premiums are used partly to buy:',
 'Units in ILP sub-funds', ['Shares in the insurer', 'Government bonds directly', 'Fixed deposits at a bank'],
 'An ILP combines life cover with investment: premiums buy units in the chosen sub-funds, and units are cancelled to pay insurance and other charges.'),
('The cash value of an investment-linked policy:',
 'Moves with the sub-funds', ['Is guaranteed by the insurer', 'Is fixed at the start', 'Is set by MAS each year'],
 "An ILP's value depends on the unit prices of its sub-funds, so it is not guaranteed and can fall. The client bears the investment risk."),
('Under MAS Notice 307, the disclosure documents for an investment-linked policy include a product summary and a:',
 'Product highlights sheet', ['Copy of its reinsurance treaty', 'Sales commission table', 'Board meeting minutes'],
 'MAS Notice 307 (para 9) requires a product summary, the policy, a policy illustration and a product highlights sheet for each ILP. FAA-N16 requires the adviser to give the client these documents before the client signs.'),
('An ILP policyholder moves money from one sub-fund to another within the same policy. This is called:',
 'Fund switching', ['Policy surrender', 'Policy loan', 'Premium holiday'],
 'Switching moves units between sub-funds in the policy. MAS Notice 307 requires the product summary to state the switching procedure and any switching fee between ILP sub-funds.'),
('Units are cancelled from an investment-linked policy mainly to pay for:',
 'Insurance and policy charges', ["The client's income tax", "The adviser's annual fee to MAS", 'Dividends to shareholders'],
 'MAS Notice 307 lists charges for insurance coverage, premium charges and other fees as payable by deduction from premiums or by cancelling units, which reduces the fund value.'),
('A unit trust in Singapore is a form of:',
 'Collective investment scheme', ['Structured deposit', 'Endowment policy', 'Fixed deposit account'],
 "A unit trust pools investors' money in a scheme run by a manager, with assets held by a trustee. The Code on Collective Investment Schemes sets standards for those offered to the public."),
('Under the Code on Collective Investment Schemes, the trustee of an authorised unit trust should be:',
 'Independent of the manager', ['A subsidiary of the manager', "The scheme's auditor", 'Appointed by SGX'],
 'Chapter 2 of the CIS Code says the trustee should be independent of the manager, and MAS authorises a scheme only if it has a trustee approved under section 289 of the SFA.'),
('A collective investment scheme constituted in Singapore and offered to the public under MAS rules is called:',
 'An authorised scheme', ['A recognised scheme', 'A restricted scheme', 'An unregistered scheme'],
 'A scheme offered to the public must be authorised by MAS if constituted in Singapore, or recognised if constituted outside Singapore. Restricted schemes are exempt and are offered only to relevant persons or at S$200,000 or more per transaction.'),
('Which document sets standards on investment limits, borrowing and operation of collective investment schemes offered to the public?',
 'The CIS Code', ['The SGX Listing Manual', 'The Insurance Act', 'The Banking Code'],
 'MAS issues the Code on Collective Investment Schemes under section 321 of the SFA. It covers the trustee and manager, dealing and valuation, and the investment guidelines and borrowing limits for authorised schemes.'),
('Under the CIS Code, the manager of an authorised scheme must deal in units at least on:',
 'One dealing day a month', ['One dealing day a year', 'One dealing day a quarter', 'Every business day'],
 'Chapter 6.1 of the CIS Code requires dealing in units in line with the constituent document and prospectus, and in any event on at least one dealing day a month.'),
("A fund's net assets are S$12 million and it has 8 million units in issue. What is the NAV per unit?",
 'S$1.50', ['S$0.67', 'S$1.25', 'S$2.00'],
 'A unit price is based on the NAV divided by the number of units outstanding: S$12 million / 8 million units = S$1.50. Dividing the other way gives S$0.67.'),
('Under Part 12 of the SFA, trading done to create a false or misleading appearance of active trading in a security is called:',
 'False trading', ['Best execution', 'Market making', 'Portfolio rebalancing'],
 'False trading is one of the market misconduct offences in Part 12 of the Securities and Futures Act 2001, alongside false or misleading statements, market manipulation and insider trading.'),
("Singapore's insider trading prohibitions are found in:",
 'The Securities and Futures Act', ['The Financial Advisers Act', 'The Companies Act 1967', 'The Penal Code'],
 'Part 12 of the Securities and Futures Act 2001 contains the market misconduct provisions, including insider trading, false trading and market manipulation.'),
('Under section 234(1A) of the SFA, an investor who lost money by relying on a false or misleading statement may claim compensation:',
 'Even if the wrongdoer made no profit', ['Only if the wrongdoer is jailed', 'Only through MAS', "Only up to the wrongdoer's profit"],
 'Section 234(1A) lets investors who relied on false or misleading statements or omissions obtain compensation whether or not the wrongdoer gained a profit or avoided a loss. For other misconduct, such as insider trading, compensation is capped at that profit or loss avoided.'),
('Spreading a rumour that a company will be taken over, to push up its share price, is:',
 'A false or misleading statement', ['Legitimate market research', 'A permitted profit forecast', 'Fair comment'],
 'Making false or misleading statements is one of the market misconduct offences in Part 12 of the SFA, as are false trading, market manipulation and insider trading.'),
('A trader buys large amounts of a thinly traded share near the close to raise its closing price. This is:',
 'Market manipulation', ['Best execution', 'Normal liquidity provision', 'Portfolio hedging'],
 "Trading to push a price up or down so as to mislead others is market manipulation, one of the market misconduct offences in Part 12 of the SFA."),
('For market misconduct under Part 12 of the SFA, MAS can take civil penalty action, and the AGC can also bring:',
 'Criminal proceedings', ['A tax assessment', 'A licence for the trader', 'An SGX listing'],
 "MAS may take civil penalty action for Part 12 market misconduct, proven on a balance of probabilities, while only the AGC can bring a criminal prosecution. The civil regime supplements the criminal one."),
('Which CPF account is mainly used for housing, education and approved investments?',
 'The Ordinary Account', ['The MediSave Account', 'The Retirement Account', 'The Special Account'],
 'Many members use the Ordinary Account to buy a property or service a housing loan, and it can also be used for approved education and, under the CPF Investment Scheme, investments. MediSave is for healthcare.'),
('Which CPF account is used mainly for hospital bills and approved medical insurance?',
 'The MediSave Account', ['The Ordinary Account', 'The Retirement Account', 'The Special Account'],
 "MediSave can be used for the member's own and dependants' hospitalisation and for approved medical insurance premiums such as MediShield Life."),
("A CPF member's Retirement Account is created at age:",
 '55', ['50', '60', '65'],
 'At 55 a Retirement Account is created and the Special Account is closed, with savings moved into the Retirement Account.'),
('CPF LIFE provides a member with:',
 'Monthly payouts for life', ['A lump sum paid at age 55', 'A one-off housing grant', 'Free term life cover'],
 'CPF LIFE is the national longevity insurance annuity scheme. It gives monthly payouts, which can start from age 65, no matter how long the member lives.'),
('Which national scheme gives basic lifelong health insurance for large hospital bills?',
 'MediShield Life', ['CPF LIFE', 'ElderShield', "Dependants' Protection Scheme"],
 'MediShield Life automatically covers all Singapore citizens and permanent residents for life, for large hospital bills and selected costly outpatient treatments such as dialysis and cancer drugs.'),
('The CPF Investment Scheme lets members invest some of their CPF savings in:',
 'Approved investment products', ['Any overseas property', 'Cryptocurrency exchanges', 'Loans to private companies'],
 'CPFIS lets members invest Ordinary Account savings above the first S$20,000 (and Special Account savings above S$40,000) in a range of approved investments, at their own risk.'),
('Which scheme gives CPF members term life cover so their families have money if they die or are permanently incapacitated?',
 "Dependants' Protection Scheme", ['CPF LIFE annuity scheme', 'MediShield Life', 'Home Protection Scheme'],
 "The Dependants' Protection Scheme is a term life insurance scheme paying out on death, terminal illness or total permanent disability. The Home Protection Scheme protects members using CPF for HDB housing loans."),
('The Home Protection Scheme mainly protects CPF members who use CPF savings to pay for:',
 'An HDB flat', ['Private car loans', 'University fees', 'Overseas holidays'],
 'The Home Protection Scheme is a mortgage-reducing insurance that pays off the outstanding HDB housing loan if the member dies, becomes terminally ill or is permanently incapacitated.'),
('A unit trust whose units are listed and traded on SGX throughout the day is an:',
 'Exchange-traded fund', ['Endowment policy', 'Deferred annuity plan', 'Structured deposit'],
 'An ETF is an investment fund listed and traded on a stock exchange, like a share. Most aim to track an index, such as the Straits Times Index.'),
("A product's prospectus for a collective investment scheme offered to the public must be:",
 'Registered with MAS', ['Approved by the CPF Board', 'Signed by every investor', 'Kept secret from investors'],
 'An offer of units in a CIS must be made in or accompanied by a MAS-registered prospectus and a product highlights sheet, unless the offer is exempt.'),
("A structured product's returns depend on derivatives linked to an index. Under FAA-N16 it is most likely a:",
 'Specified Investment Product', ['Excluded Investment Product', 'Basic savings product', 'Plain whole life policy'],
 'Under FAA-N16, only products in the Annex 1 list (simple capital markets products in the prescribed schedule, non-ILP life policies and qualifying ILP sub-funds) are Excluded Investment Products. A derivative-linked structured product is generally a Specified Investment Product, which calls for a CKA or CAR.'),
('A key difference between an ILP and a buy term and invest separately approach is that an ILP:',
 'Bundles cover and investing', ['Has no insurance charges', 'Guarantees the fund value', 'Cannot be surrendered'],
 'An ILP bundles life cover and investment in one policy. Buying term cover and investing separately keeps the two apart, which can make costs easier to compare.'),
('Dollar cost averaging through a regular premium ILP means the client:',
 'Buys more units when cheap', ['Always buys at the lowest price', 'Pays no charges', 'Gets a guaranteed return'],
 'A fixed regular amount buys more units when prices fall and fewer when they rise, which smooths the average cost but does not guarantee a profit.'),
]
